==Icelandic==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|svangr||slender, slim, thin|lang=non}} from {{term|svangi||the groins|lang=non}}, also spelled {{term|svangr|lang=non}}. Compare the German {{term|schlank|lang=de}}.

====Adjective====
{{is-adj-01|svöng|svangt|svengri|33=svangari|svengstur|44=svangastur}}

# [[hungry]]
#: ''Ertu '''svöng'''?''
#:: Are you '''hungry'''?
#: ''Ég er mjög '''svangur'''.''
#:: I'm really '''hungry'''.

=====Derived terms=====
* [[ég er svangur]] ([[I am hungry]])

=====See also=====
* [[svengja]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|is}} from {{term|svangi|lang=non}} which was also spelled {{term|svangr|lang=non}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|m|svangs|svangar}}

# used in set phrases
#: ''Ég held að ég [[fá sér í svanginn|fái mér eitthvað í '''svanginn''']].''
#:: I think I'll get something to eat.

=====Usage notes=====
* This word is in modern Icelandic, mostly used in the [[accusative case]] with a [[definite article]] ("[[svanginn]]"); almost only in the phrase {{term|fá sér í svanginn|fá sér eitthvað í svanginn|to get something to eat|lang=is}}.

=====Derived terms=====
* [[fá sér í svanginn]] (to get something to eat)

